From 69f6c5eb7ca042ecb42787cf733f3678c08ab945 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreyash Damanwala <shreyash.damanwala@nxp.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:51:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: endpoint: Add configurable iKVM display and KVM
 modes

Add runtime KVM configuration support to the i.MX9 VGA PCIe endpoint function.

* Read display resolution and KVM mode from /etc/kvm.conf.
* Support 1080p and 4K display configurations.
* Select the appropriate fallback EDID based on the configured mode.
* Parse monitor EDID to determine the maximum supported resolution.
* Detect ADV7535 and LT9611UXC display bridges from device tree.
* Select the appropriate Option ROM for PCIe video or PCIe KVM mode.
* Initialize the HID BAR only when PCIe KVM mode is enabled.
* Restart the obmc-ikvm service after endpoint initialization.
* Move the i.MX9 VGA EPF build target into the iKVM subdirectory.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Shreyash Damanwala <shreyash.damanwala@nxp.com>
